      "routine": "(4 actions) The trap loses 1 action per disabled channel each turn. On each action, a different channel spews lava, dealing 4d6 fire damage to each creature within 10 feet of the channel (check (reflex, dc:27, basic) save), and increasing the depth of the lava in the room by 1 foot (4 feet per round if all the channels are active).\nA creature that starts its turn in lava takes 8d6 fire damage and is Immobilized until it Escapes the hardening lava (DC 27). The creature might suffocate if covered in lava.\nLava from the previous round hardens fully at the start of the trap's turn, effectively raising the floor of the room. Once the room is full of lava, the trap stops taking actions, but creatures in the room remain stuck until the floor opens and the trap resets.",
