          "id": "bfmkqrbi3vcWnEQ8",
          "name": "Hunt Prey",
          "kind": "action",
          "description": "The slave lord designates as its prey a single creature that they can see or hear or that they are Tracking. They gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Perception checks when they Seek their prey and a +2 circumstance bonus to Track their prey. They also ignore the penalty for making ranged attacks within their second range increment against their prey.\nThe first time a slave lord hits their hunted prey in a round, they deal 2d8 additional precision damage. A slave lord can have only one prey designated at a time.",
